## T3.7 — Desk respects cognitive `Sideline` for entries only

Implemented R8 cognitive gating in the desk playbook dispatch path: entries are skipped when `memory.Sideline(symbol)` is true; exits always reach `desk.SubmitAction`.

### Implementation

**`trader/desk_cycle.go`** — gate before submit:

```56:78:trader/desk_cycle.go
	for _, action := range sortActionsExitsFirst(crypto.story.Actions()) {
		if action == nil {
			continue
		}

		if !crypto.shouldSubmitPlaybookAction(action) {
			continue
		}

		errnie.Error(crypto.desk.SubmitAction(action, holdings))
	}
}

func (crypto *Crypto) shouldSubmitPlaybookAction(action *logic.Action) bool {
	if action.Type.IsExit() {
		return true
	}

	if crypto.memory == nil {
		return true
	}

	return !crypto.memory.Sideline(action.Symbol)
}
```

**Tests** — `TestCryptoApplyPlaybookActionsRespectsSideline` in `desk_cycle_test.go`; shared helpers moved to `desk_cycle_helpers_test.go` (files stay ≤400 lines).

